## Durable rules

- Record identity proof, session or token lifecycle, authorization boundaries, and privilege changes when applicable.
- Keep secret values outside source and documentation; record only approved storage and rotation rules.
- Identify sensitive data, purpose, access, retention, deletion obligations, and disclosure boundaries.
- Record relevant threats, mitigations, residual risks, audit evidence, and incident ownership.
- Link requirements to actual controls and tests; do not claim compliance from intention alone.

